<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:55Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Third-country removals: Trump’s deportation policy by the numbers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d3473cb03c2bb5be6788dd0850a2edeb5bc9d4cd21d07031ff7817b4819e8c2</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T05:04:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-third-country-removals-trump-deportation-policy-numbers--6d700771bc51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-third-country-removals-trump-deportation-policy-numbers" /><summary type="html">Since January 2025, the Trump administration has deported more than 25,000 people to so-called “third countries” – places that are not their countries of origin. Working with a team of 26 international media outlets, Forbidden Stories and FRANCE 24 have used information gathered by NGOs and open-source information to count and map these deportations. Our investigation shines a light on the scale of this mass deportation campaign that is being carried out under the cover of darkness.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>ICE, Trump and Africa: Secret deals, broken lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a33bbc7b860744775206950f50ea340845b0b7990e3a4d7cf9e426f2776480b2</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T05:00:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260921-ice-trump-and-africa-secret-deals-broken-lives--a4dce10e3903.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260921-ice-trump-and-africa-secret-deals-broken-lives" /><summary type="html">For this edition of Reporters+, Karina Chabour has investigated a dark side of Donald Trump’s immigration policy. How ICE deports immigrants to so-called ‘third countries’ in Africa, far from the United States and often far from their countries of origin.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>‘Waiting for us to crack’: In Cameroon, the victims of Trump’s deportations face uncertain fates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff1a37690f6b2f04ac7216521bb70d54f2b70fc998e471022ef773390c900c5b</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T05:00:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260921-waiting-for-us-to-crack-victims-of-trump-deportations-face-uncertain-fates-in-cameroon--49f56fccb149.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260921-waiting-for-us-to-crack-victims-of-trump-deportations-face-uncertain-fates-in-cameroon" /><summary type="html">Under often-secret deals struck with so-called "third countries" across Africa and Latin America, US President Donald Trump has deported thousands of people hoping to build new lives in the US to countries they’ve never set foot in before. Together with Forbidden Stories, FRANCE 24 investigated the stories of several African migrants housed in a temporary shelter in Cameroon’s capital Yaoundé whose lives have been thrown into chaos by their abrupt deportation from the US.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Deported to Africa: An international investigation into Trump’s migrant policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e3bc80f93b8d32c09936e45b0de4acd3fbb055cb68775adb51ee7ec9a2ebf15</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T05:00:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260921-deported-to-africa-an-international-investigation-into-trump-s-migrant-policy--a08a651759dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260921-deported-to-africa-an-international-investigation-into-trump-s-migrant-policy" /><summary type="html">As part of a consortium of 26 media outlets coordinated by Forbidden Stories, FRANCE 24 and RFI spent seven months investigating the secret deals struck between the administration of US President Donald Trump and several African countries. These so-called “third countries” have agreed to host undocumented migrants detained by ICE and deported from the US.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Putin's party dominates in elections, Moscow vows revenge after massive drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b1981ccc4a61a11f3ee3fa550da0fe3094f455980cba04ae192b8bb704c3e0</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T02:28:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-live-united-russia-dominates-in-elections-moscow-vows-revenge-after-massive-drone-attack--f60c32e623c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-live-united-russia-dominates-in-elections-moscow-vows-revenge-after-massive-drone-attack" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin's ruling United Russia party won a large majority in the country's parliamentary elections, marked by cyberattacks and a barrage of Ukrainian drone strikes, according to results published by state media early Monday. Meanwhile, Moscow has vowed to "intensify" its strikes on Kyiv in response to the massive drone attack on the Russian capital. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US, China discuss AI safety ahead of Trump-Xi summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abef6bc27d3ec7c600d988e55bd115f159713bbe819eb933bb4439b37df95307</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T02:22:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-china-discuss-ai-safety-ahead-of-trump-xi-summit--f6aa3899454b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-china-discuss-ai-safety-ahead-of-trump-xi-summit" /><summary type="html">US and Chinese officials discussed creating a mechanism to communicate over potentially serious AI incidents during talks in New York on Sunday, as the two sides sought progress on technology and trade ahead of this week’s Trump-Xi summit.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Macron, Carney hail new chapter in France-Canada ties at symbolic archipelago meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8019a1e7af6dd096876e1344db39eaeaf970d1477d543d2648b3dbabaf79b62</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T02:16:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-macron-and-carney-hail-new-chapter-in-france-canada-ties-at-symbolic-archipelago-meeting--b31e9a09c8fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-macron-and-carney-hail-new-chapter-in-france-canada-ties-at-symbolic-archipelago-meeting" /><summary type="html">French President ​Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney on ​Sunday called for stronger bilateral ties in the face of new global threats at a meeting on Saint Pierre and Miquelon, a French territory off Canada's Newfoundland. The first-ever visit by a Canadian leader to the North Atlantic archipelago came as both countries have increasingly awkward relations with the US.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands protest in France against bill expanding protections for police use of force</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0408082dc510eee03b413b6975fae524615aaf1f9edf630d1d317be79abedfd5</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T23:56:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260920-thousands-protest-in-france-against-bill-expanding-protections-for-police-use-of-force--19eae3f93fb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260920-thousands-protest-in-france-against-bill-expanding-protections-for-police-use-of-force" /><summary type="html">Thousands marched across France on Sunday against a bill that would presume police officers acted lawfully when using their weapons, a measure critics have denounced as a 'licence to kill.'</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Torres strikes again as PSG beat bitter rivals Marseille 2-1</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8406dbc621abaf91dba69f07e79cc8f9a7418627e7e3064d13adf38781dc4792</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T21:55:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260920-torres-strikes-again-as-psg-beat-bitter-rivals-marseille-2-1--fb2a93223bd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260920-torres-strikes-again-as-psg-beat-bitter-rivals-marseille-2-1" /><summary type="html">Paris Saint-Germain claimed the bragging rights in 'Le Classique' on Sunday, edging Marseille 2-1 as Spaniard Ferran Torres scored his seventh goal in six appearances for his new club.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's ruling party on track to win election after Ukraine's drone attacks on Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f6e0c2e365aa3856443c9e2a0d0ee0b0892c6c1e0f5dc4250a0e85432b49b2b</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T20:14:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-russia-s-ruling-party-on-track-to-win-election-after-ukraine-s-drone-attacks-on-moscow--ec6bb665f16d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-russia-s-ruling-party-on-track-to-win-election-after-ukraine-s-drone-attacks-on-moscow" /><summary type="html">Russia's ruling United Russia party on Sunday was projected to win the country's tightly controlled parliamentary elections, according to exit polls. Ukraine launched a massive drone attack on Moscow, killing three people, said city officials, on the third and final day of Russia's wartime vote.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macron, Carney hail new chapter in France-Canada ties at symbolic archipelago meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35e55d40bcfc67cabc3285026311155c18f914dc4f6a53a8bff560a004764983</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T18:29:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260920-macron-carney-hail-new-chapter-in-france-canada-ties-at-symbolic-archipelago-meeting--b50fb442cea3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260920-macron-carney-hail-new-chapter-in-france-canada-ties-at-symbolic-archipelago-meeting" /><summary type="html">French President ​Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney on ​Sunday called for stronger bilateral ties in the face of new global threats at a meeting on Saint Pierre and Miquelon, a French territory off Canada's Newfoundland. The first-ever visit by a Canadian leader to the North Atlantic archipelago came as both countries have increasingly awkward relations with the US.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Replay: Macron, Carney hail new chapter on France-Canada ties at St. Pierre and Miquelon meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfb75767712f8859cbf3fecfd78f42310db3961c0c2eb9f3b2515fbf1db866c8</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T18:24:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-macron-carney-hail-new-chapter-on-france-canada-ties-at-st-pierre-and-miquelon-meeting--e8078b25086f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-macron-carney-hail-new-chapter-on-france-canada-ties-at-st-pierre-and-miquelon-meeting" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said France and Canada were "two great independent nations who want to stay that way" in a joint news conference with Canadian leader Mark Carney Sunday. Watch the press conference by the two leaders on the French overseas territory of Saint Pierre and Miquelon just off Canada's Atlantic coast.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Merz vows to "push on despite setbacks"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6eee02bb97664e028837f3f2bcc1e2a8b8b60f3fe01341ea34c3d8b4b82b29e8</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T17:20:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260920-germany-merz-vows-to-push-on-despite-setbacks--299c10596752.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260920-germany-merz-vows-to-push-on-despite-setbacks" /><summary type="html">German voters have delivered a fresh setback to Chancellor Friedrich Merz in two key regional elections.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>The Deportation Project: Inside the Trump administration's secret deals to expel people worldwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20549cf932d5e5fae733c0adef5b02f98c184ada354bd1c7ee9cc948655f62f7</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T17:08:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260920-the-deportation-project-inside-the-trump-administration-s-secret-deals-to-expel-people-worl--8f166565a178.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260920-the-deportation-project-inside-the-trump-administration-s-secret-deals-to-expel-people-worldwide" /><summary type="html">A consortium of 72 journalists from 26 media outlets coordinated by Forbidden Stories have been working on the Deportation Project for months. On Monday, we will take you inside the Trump administration's secret deals to expel people worldwide.</summary></entry><entry><title>Exit polls show 'disaster' for Merz' CDU party in two state elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76c871cb2ba43623019cba6d79b22f5959da2d7ea596bf471595f745a81b61d2</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T16:54:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/exit-polls-show-disaster-for-merz-cdu-party-in-two-state-elections--c7c3b264c875.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/exit-polls-show-disaster-for-merz-cdu-party-in-two-state-elections" /><summary type="html">Germans headed to the polls today in two state elections - in Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. Exit polls suggest a dramatic loss for the Chancellor Freidrich Mertz's Christian Democratic Union party. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Berlin, Jörg Taszman.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Merz admits ‘disaster’ in state elections, vows to press ahead with reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b61ebf8f2c7720e2cb5a8455bb2161b95fbe2cb3f168c0f68ff1301754a447f6</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T16:23:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-strong-gains-in-two-state-elections--6ffdab729532.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-strong-gains-in-two-state-elections" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz on Sunday described his CDU party's heavy losses in two regional elections as a "disaster", but vowed to push ahead with a reform drive. The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party took first place in ​the northeastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, exit polls showed, and also gained in strength in another election in Berlin.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli settler and Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd7b129dc479994cb50636284709b631027221bbf4b6685d5386caa8adfc2fc2</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T15:30:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings--6ec13ca89571.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings" /><summary type="html">A suspected Palestinian gunman on Sunday shot dead an Israeli man near a West Bank settlement, according to Israeli officials. The gunman was located at a Ramallah hospital and arrested, police said. Elsewhere in the West Bank, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian motorist who the military said was attempting to run them over. The flare up in violence came on the eve of the Jewish holy day of Yom Kippur.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>AfD threatens fresh blow to Merz: Two German states hold key vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3b87d22ac10e3198edc20a8efd41a99b938f97aa3b3cc92e3b6d8dae21c80d3</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:56:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/afd-threatens-fresh-blow-to-merz-two-german-states-hold-key-vote--61567b7062b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/afd-threatens-fresh-blow-to-merz-two-german-states-hold-key-vote" /><summary type="html">Two German states are heading to the polls today – in Berlin and the state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. The far-right AfD party is expected to make further gains after securing a historic win in Saxony-Anhalt two weeks ago, though it has no realistic path to power in Berlin. Sunday's vote is a key test for Chancellor Friedrich Merz, one that could determine whether he can hold on to power. Details with Jamie Smith-Maillet, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine fires over 1,000 drones at Russia in "largest ever" attack on Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81f0bff8bf5e66f937a41323757897961cb0561992d6a5bd2d9a46d56f7c9da8</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:46:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-fires-over-1-000-drones-at-russia-in-largest-ever-attack-on-moscow--fd9c5d810d0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-fires-over-1-000-drones-at-russia-in-largest-ever-attack-on-moscow" /><summary type="html">Russia is completing its three-day vote for the Duma this Sunday – the first since its large-scale invasion of Ukraine. The election was organised for the first time also in the Ukrainian regions occupied by Russia, and it was marked by Ukrainian drone strikes at various areas - mainly Moscow. Details by Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>An Israeli settler and a Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81512ab0c0d1cb7f6825d24c7a47f477fd862f12c7cddc0f2f1ffdad6054fa95</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:34:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/an-israeli-settler-and-a-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings--7750aafd0f5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/an-israeli-settler-and-a-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings" /><summary type="html">An Israeli settler has been fatally shot in the occupied West Bank, while Israel's military said it killed a man who attempted to ram his vehicle into troops elsewhere in the Palestinian territory. The news came as violence in the West Bank is escalating at a very rapid pace. “All Israeli military authorities involved with the West Bank have been warning the Israeli government that the situation is basically out of control”, explains FRANCE 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran closes French language centre in Tehran for ‘illegal acts’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71176e697fbdcf3ea02dac465be44154898931f6c41052e9a3f797588ab70374</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T13:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-iran-closes-french-language-centre-in-tehran-for-illegal-acts--e9366397fe37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-iran-closes-french-language-centre-in-tehran-for-illegal-acts" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities on Sunday shut down the French Language Centre (CLF) in Tehran, alleging the French embassy-linked institute conducted "illegal acts that violated diplomatic conventions" and "abused its status as a language training facility". France has vowed to take "appropriate measures" in response.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Syria protests, Céline Dion on stage and Quito wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43c0892503fdd85d0edf644ddcc1c26e5343c9918f4833d2be6ec804a54cab14</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T13:15:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-the-week-in-pictures-syria-protests-c_line-dion-on-stage-and-quito-wildfires--7c494f9fc87e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-the-week-in-pictures-syria-protests-c%C3%A9line-dion-on-stage-and-quito-wildfires" /><summary type="html">From protests against rising fuel prices in Syria to Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney’s EU charm offensive to Quito’s wildfires and Céline Dion’s return to the stage, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks and no Western support: What are Saudi Arabia's options ?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5af2e0c44e7cc5567fc30d0b7969b149bc3bfca53dd005ded96dd970080b6c87</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:24:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options--12b32e145452.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options" /><summary type="html">The US has warned that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthis could rapidly escalate. It comes after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The Houthis' lightning offensive seized swathes of Yemeni territory in recent weeks and has left hundreds dead. In the face of such attacks and with no support from its American ally, what are Saudi Arabia’s options?</summary></entry><entry><title>'NAZA' documentary about Gaza war sparks political storm in Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d7fa08580bad2c9c2ca309c1cf3709e1e6306a5433a0a24aa7213ab37f01e9f</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:22:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel--e9ca19249009.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel" /><summary type="html">The Israeli filmmakers behind the documentary NAZA may have received a standing ovation at the Venice film festival, they have been facing violent threats to their lives and citizenship at home in Israel. A month ahead of crucial elections, the film profiles anonymous military sources who speak about the widespread killing of civilians in Gaza. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he intends to introduce legislation aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers". Details by Shirli Sitbon, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.</summary></entry></feed>
